# Styling: arbitrary CSS in the same file only

When adding or changing UI styles in this project, put styles in the **same file** you are editing (usually the `.tsx` component). Do not spread one-off styles into global SCSS or new style files.

## Do

- Use Tailwind arbitrary values inline on `className` in the component being changed
- Reuse existing utility / theme classes when they already match (`var(--primary)`, `text-[var(--black)]`, etc.)
- Keep layout and spacing tweaks colocated with the markup they affect

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — styles live in the component file
<section className="w-full py-[40px]">
  <div className="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1320px] px-[15px]">
    <h2 className="mb-0 text-[24px] font-bold leading-[1.2] text-[#1a1a1a]">
```

## Don't

- Do **not** add or edit files under `public/assets/scss/` for component-specific tweaks
- Do **not** create new `.scss`, `.css`, or CSS module files for one-off layout/spacing/color changes
- Do **not** add inline `style={{ ... }}` when a Tailwind arbitrary class can express the same thing
- Do **not** refactor unrelated legacy SCSS unless the task explicitly asks for it

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — don't fix spacing by editing _pop-up.scss or _cart.scss
// ❌ BAD — don't add a new ShopDetails.module.scss for a single margin tweak
```

## Scope

- **New work**: arbitrary Tailwind in the component file, every time
- **Existing SCSS classes**: leave them alone unless the task is specifically to migrate or fix that stylesheet
- **Shared design tokens**: prefer `var(--*)` and existing project classes over hard-coded hex when a token already exists
